WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.770
The client's interviews are in the project

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.657
DeliR extracts statements from the interviews

00:00:13.707 --> 00:00:24.978
Every statement has its verified quote

00:00:25.028 --> 00:00:35.017
Sources are compared with each other

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:45.469
Conflicting versions surface right away

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:56.173
Ask DeliR to rebuild the process

00:00:56.223 --> 00:01:03.138
DeliR reads the sources and extracts the facts

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:09.726
The answer quotes people: nothing invented

00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:22.969
What nobody says becomes an open question

00:01:22.419 --> 00:01:33.266
The As-Is in BPMN 2.0: 2 lanes, 5 activities

00:01:33.316 --> 00:01:42.746
The diagram matches the sources: 100%

00:01:42.796 --> 00:01:59.481
Each element shows its supporting quote

00:01:59.531 --> 00:02:15.175
Every version stays tracked

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:26.401
To-Be hypotheses come from the people doing the work

00:02:26.451 --> 00:02:35.176
Each proposal carries its own quotes

00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:40.896
Simulating today's process (As-Is)

00:02:40.946 --> 00:02:46.394
Requests flow through the process

00:02:46.444 --> 00:02:53.394
The queue builds up at “Approve spend”

00:02:53.444 --> 00:03:12.576
Six KPIs update as the simulation runs

00:03:12.026 --> 00:03:20.867
The heatmap shows where requests wait

00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:30.868
Bottleneck: 1d 9h average wait

00:03:30.318 --> 00:03:38.108
To-Be: complete request and a daily delegate

00:03:38.158 --> 00:03:44.107
Same requests, no queue at approval

00:03:44.157 --> 00:04:00.268
The same six KPIs, in the new process

00:03:59.718 --> 00:04:11.186
To-Be: cycle time −95%, cost per case −43%

00:04:11.236 --> 00:04:16.871
Simulated values, not guaranteed results

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:29.327
DeliR checks the work is complete

00:04:29.377 --> 00:04:42.035
The process owner gets a read-only dashboard

00:04:42.085 --> 00:04:46.793
From interviews to decision, with numbers
